              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for a rainstorm, then the Telugu for to lose strength."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: పిడుగు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పిడుగు — piḍugu — \"a thunderbolt; a lightning strike\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పొలంలో తాటిచెట్టు మీద పిడుగు పడింది. polaṁlō tāṭiceṭṭu mīda piḍugu paḍindi. Lightning struck a palm tree in the field."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పిడుగు (piḍugu) పడు, lightning strikes. Bad news that comes out of nowhere is also a పిడుగు (piḍugu)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పిడుగు (piḍugu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 4150 lists Telugu piḍugu, \"a thunderbolt, lightning\", with Kannada piḍugu."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
