          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కమ్ము — kammu — \"to close in; to envelop\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఆకాశంలో నల్లని మబ్బులు కమ్మాయి. ākāśaṁlō nallani mabbulu kammāyi. Dark clouds closed in across the sky."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (it …): కమ్మింది, kammindi."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Said of clouds, smoke or darkness that cover everything. Its subject is a thing, so the past shown is the third person: కమ్మింది, it closed in."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కమ్ము (kammu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 1221 lists Telugu kammu, \"to cover, to surround, to overspread\", beside kappu, \"to spread over in a thick covering, as clouds\"."
            }
          ]
